{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784301142,"nonce":"oVZ2ZGQQHqTJQK3Dr6TUMDOub0w=","title":"[dogfood] /.scarab gitignore blocks committing the pipeline config","message":"The repo's .gitignore has a blanket `/.scarab` (to ignore the local object-store fallback at ./.scarab/objects). But a repo declares its CI at `.scarab/*.yaml` — the exact path the server enumerates. So the documented pipeline path is uncommittable out of the box: `git add .scarab/ci.yaml` silently does nothing.\n\nFound while dogfooding (adding .scarab/ci.yaml to this repo). Fixed on branch dogfood/scarab-ci-pipeline by narrowing the ignore to `/.scarab/*` with negations for `*.yaml`/`*.yml`/`lib/`. Consider shipping that .gitignore in the repo template / docs so downstream repos don't hit it.","files":null}]}